{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ERyoRrDPtX2at1BAj6qrj3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets), `docs/` (specifications).\n\n**Current state of implementation:**\n- `pkg/sys/` — **exists** (source code provided: stat.go, stat_darwin.go, stat_linux.go, terminal.go)\n- `pkg/format/` — **exists** (source code provided: color.go, size.go, table.go)\n- `pkg/testutils/` — **no source code on working branch** (specs complete, code was generated in prior pipeline run but only at generation-merged tags)\n- `magefiles/` — excluded from generation scope (DD7)\n\n**Current release: 00.0** (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure)\n- rel00.0-uc001-magefiles — excluded by DD7\n- rel00.0-uc002-format — already implemented (source exists)\n- rel00.0-uc003-sys — already implemented (source exists)\n- rel00.0-uc004-testutils — **not started, only viable remaining work**\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe only remaining work for release 00.0 is `pkg/testutils/`. This is the differential testing harness — the foundational verification component that all `cmd/` packages depend on. It must exist before any utility can be verified.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/testutils DiffTest struct and differential test runner\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component description, data structures section for DiffTest, design decision DD2 on differential testing, DD6 on LC_ALL=C)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (testutils PRD with full requirement details -- verify exact filename by listing docs/specs/product-requirements/ for the testutils PRD)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (use case describing end-to-end testutils execution path)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (release 00.0 test suite covering testutils acceptance)\n      - go.mod (verify module path and golang.org/x/sys dependency availability)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"DiffTest struct (test case definition), TestResult struct (comparison outcome), Run function (execute both binaries and compare), normalization hook support\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define exported DiffTest struct with fields for: Go binary path, reference binary path, command-line arguments ([]string), stdin input ([]byte or io.Reader), environment variables ([]string), and description/name for reporting. Define exported TestResult struct with fields for: pass/fail status, stdout from each binary, stderr from each binary, exit code from each binary, and a human-readable divergence summary when outputs differ.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement a Run function (or DiffTest method) that executes both the Go binary and the reference GNU binary with identical stdin, arguments, and environment. Capture stdout, stderr, and exit code from each invocation. Use os/exec.Command for binary execution.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement comparison logic that checks stdout, stderr, and exit code between Go binary output and reference binary output. Comparison is byte-for-byte by default. When outputs diverge, populate TestResult with the input that triggered the divergence, the expected output (reference binary), and the actual output (Go binary).\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support normalization functions (type NormalizeFunc func([]byte) []byte) that are applied to stdout and stderr before comparison. Normalization hooks are optional per-DiffTest and allow known acceptable differences (e.g., timestamps, path prefixes) to be filtered before byte comparison. DiffTest holds a slice of normalization functions.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go -- named after the primary exported type DiffTest, not the package name, per project convention that forbids testutils/testutils.go.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Package name is testutils per ARCHITECTURE.yaml component definition.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Run must inject LC_ALL=C into the environment for both binary executions per ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD6. This ensures Go and reference binary outputs agree on string ordering and character classification. If the caller-provided environment already sets LC_ALL, the injected value takes precedence.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/... succeeds with no compilation errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no warnings.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"DiffTest struct is exported with all fields needed to fully specify a differential test case: binary paths, args, stdin, env, and normalization hooks.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Run function is exported, executes both binaries with identical inputs, and returns a TestResult indicating pass/fail with stdout, stderr, exit code from each binary and a divergence summary on mismatch.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":41352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68860b32-0d72-4592-a385-b521db329a30","uuid":"195b2f69-d6cc-439a-b953-d84cffe613fa"}
